{{!--
  ONE CAUGHT FIGURE'S MATH, COLLAPSED — the per-figure disclosure the spread and blast resolution cards
  carry under each row (user ruling 2026-08-28, option A). Included as a partial from both cards so the
  markup, like the rows themselves, exists once.

  Context = the `breakdown` object combat/damage-breakdown.js `cardBreakdownFor` builds:
    { summary, blocks: [{ index, multi, rows: [{ label, value, drain }] }] }
  `summary` and every label/value arrive PRE-LOCALIZED from JS (the GasCloudPenaltyClause idiom), so this
  file states no strings of its own and needs no CPLocal call.

  ⛔ NO `open` ATTRIBUTE, EVER. Collapsed by default is the ruling itself — a five-victim card has to
  stay scannable — and the keeper asserts the rendered DOM carries no `open`.

  `multi` marks a figure that took more than one round: each round is its own trip through the armour
  pipeline (SP is subtracted per hit, and a barrier's pool falls between them), so N rounds are N blocks
  under one summary and each is numbered.
--}}
<details class="cp-area-breakdown">
  <summary>{{breakdown.summary}}</summary>
  {{#each breakdown.blocks}}
    {{#if this.multi}}<div class="cp-area-breakdown-index">{{this.index}}</div>{{/if}}
    {{#each this.rows}}
    <div class="cp-area-breakdown-row{{#if this.drain}} cp-area-breakdown-drain{{/if}}">
      <span class="cp-area-breakdown-label">{{this.label}}</span>
      <span class="cp-area-breakdown-value">{{this.value}}</span>
    </div>
    {{/each}}
  {{/each}}
</details>
